    "statement": "Effect receipts retain identity headers, a payload digest and allocated order without payload bytes or occurrence time. Receipt insertion and effect/relation sequence allocation use the caller's transaction and roll back together. Header comparison reports kind, subject type, subject ID, actor and payload version in that order; store adapters separately compare canonical payload digests and classify equivalent or divergent retries. Duplicate prechecks do not consume sequence positions. Optional relation positions remain SQL NULL when absent; receipt SQL errors retain their driver causes."
